# The repository is stored with LF endings and every file hash in a
# module manifest is computed over the LF form. A Windows checkout
# with `core.autocrlf=true` would otherwise rewrite the working tree to
# CRLF, and the manifests would no longer match the files.
#
# `text=auto` lets Git detect text files itself; `eol=lf` keeps the
# working tree in the same form as the repository. Binary files are
# listed explicitly so their bytes are never touched.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.whl binary
*.pyc binary
